Julia-1 decisions Android sample

This sample ports the host side of litert-community/Julia-1-LiteRT (tokenizer,
request builder, token table lookup and decoder) to Kotlin for LiteRT and
provides a Compose/MVVM application. The request contract follows the Julia
runtime in SupersonicLabs/Julia-1 by Supersonic Labs, whose model artifacts are
released under the Apache License 2.0.
https://huggingface.co/SupersonicLabs/Julia-1
Checkpoint revision: a85b127321d580d65176c89ced8273f305745d85

Model conversion changes (in the model repository): static windows of 512 and
1,024 tokens, host-side token embedding lookup from a float16 table, baked
rotary tables and attention band, the question type as a one-hot matmul, and
LayerNorm and mask rewrites that are exact in fp32. The act head is not
included. The checkpoint tokenizer is unchanged.

The encoder derives from mmBERT-small, declared MIT by its model card.
Attribution: Johns Hopkins Center for Language and Speech Processing (JHU CLSP).
https://huggingface.co/jhu-clsp/mmBERT-small
The model repository supplies no separate copyright notice or LICENSE. The
declared MIT permission text and this attribution are preserved without
inventing a copyright holder or year.

Tokenizer behavior is ported against Hugging Face tokenizers; its Apache License
2.0 text is retained. Python packages are reference tools and are not embedded
in this Android application.
https://github.com/huggingface/tokenizers

